claim_principal: "harness:codex#96ff8a24670431caf98d1225"
author: "harness:claude-code"
estimated_minutes: 300
acceptance_criteria: "Two concurrent agents of the same harness resolve to distinct claim principals without either agent setting an identity flag, so the second pm claim on a held item is refused exactly as it is for two distinct PM_AUTHOR values. The resolved session identifier is carried into the history entry alongside agent_harness and agent_model so a completed stream can attribute a mutation to one agent process. Taking over an existing live claim is never silent: it either fails or reports the prior holder and requires --force, including when the prior holder shares the caller's harness. A regression test runs two same-harness claims against one item and asserts the second is refused, and asserts the history entries carry distinct agent identifiers."
parent: pm-dj98
risk: medium
confidence: high
resolution: Automatic claims now compare a privacy-safe session-derived instance principal and history records that hashed instance.
expected_result: Same-harness agents without PM_AUTHOR are distinct claim principals and durable mutations are attributable without exposing session IDs.
actual_result: Packed consumer session B is refused with already_claimed_by after session A claims; focused regressions cover provenance and force semantics.
